        "original_id": "2665406e-ac14-5086-b574-52295b4cb0ca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Llewellyn, Hector Hugh Munro, Saki\n- Works: Green, Green My Valley Now, When William Came\n- Roles: British novelist, British writer\n\nFacts:\n- Hector Hugh Munro, better known by the pen name Saki and also as H. H. Munro, was born on 18 December 1870 and died on 14 November 1916.\n- In November 1913, Saki published the novel When William Came: A Story of London Under the Hohenzollerns.\n- Saki was a British writer whose witty, mischievous, and sometimes macabre stories satirized Edwardian society and culture.\n- Richard Dafydd Vivian Llewellyn Lloyd, known by the pen name Richard Llewellyn, was born on 8 December 1906 and died on 30 November 1983.\n- Richard Llewellyn was a British novelist.\n- In 1975, Richard Llewellyn published the novel Green, Green My Valley Now.",
